From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:49:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] Add the user manual, examples and 0.3.0 measurements

Add docs/user-manual.md with a complete model, schema, status, budget,
API and CLI reference and runnable examples; release_checks.py now runs
the manual's Python blocks as well as the tutorial's. Add application
and optimization examples (SciPy, fcmaes CMA-ES ask/tell, fcmaes BiteOpt
with deadlock penalties) under examples/python with recorded outputs,
and a Rust score_matrix example. The benchmark gains a breakdown probe
and a CRAFT_WORKERS override; the evidence adds the cumulative 0.2.0
comparison, time breakdown, worker scaling, instruction profile and
monitored-budget measurements. README and tutorial describe the matrix
API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
